  "variableMeasured": [
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "mode",
      "value": "code_lab"
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "description",
      "value": "[auto-routed: surprise=1.00] Create a Python script that implements the bootstrap rigidity test for neural networks. The script will: (1) generate synthetic constraint functions with known intrinsic dimensionality (low-dim = rigid, high-dim = fat), (2) train small feedforward networks of varying widths w, (3) measure N_c(w) as the minimum width needed to achieve zero violations on held-out constraints for each constraint sample count w, (4) output the (w, N_c(w)) table and plot. This directly tests the hypothesis that low intrinsic dimensionality causes N_c(w) to plateau after w_c. The script will be self-contained and runnable without external physics tools."
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "skill",
      "value": "None"
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "expected_prediction",
      "value": "For low-dimensional constraint manifolds (rigid), N_c(w) will rise initially then plateau at a value near the intrinsic dimension after w_c, supporting the hypothesis. For high-dimensional manifolds (fat), N_c(w) will continue increasing with w, showing no plateau. The script will produce a clear bifurcation plot demonstrating this distinction."
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "prediction_inputs"
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "target_files"
    },
    {
